\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Where ``real'' comes from. The cable is photographed, segmented in HSV, traced along its own centreline, and scaled by the known clamp separation --- giving a millimetre-accurate ground truth with no tape measure. Two independent photographs of this cable agree on its length to 0.32\nobreakspace  {}mm.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Every approach, the exact mathematics (dashed) and the real cable (dotted) on one axis. They bracket the real cable; the spread is boundary-condition modelling, not solver bugs.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
